<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.12">
  <POU Name="F_BronkhorstMFM_ILK" Id="{3f1a5d70-0b2c-4d51-9a64-7c11e2b90a03}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_BronkhorstMFM_ILK - site interlock permit for FB_BronkhorstMFM.

    PURPOSE
        Single home for every interlock condition that permits a Bronkhorst
        mass flow meter/controller to accept a non-zero flow setpoint.

    USAGE
        Evaluated by the deployment that owns the meter and wired into
        FB_BronkhorstMFM.i_xILK. The block itself never evaluates a site
        condition; it forces the flow command to zero whenever this permit is
        FALSE.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Replace the previous design, where the reusable block had no permit
          input at all and nothing could block a flow command.
        - Fail safe: an unhealthy gas panel node returns FALSE, so the commanded
          flow is held at zero.
        - Keep the condition in one function so it can be reviewed and tested
          without instantiating the meter.

    HISTORY
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Function created while adding the external interlock permit to
            FB_BronkhorstMFM (audit finding #1159, convention conv_0121ae615346).
*)
FUNCTION F_BronkhorstMFM_ILK : BOOL
VAR_INPUT
    i_xPanelFieldbusOK : BOOL; // Gas panel EtherCAT sync unit healthy (ST_M3DeviceBaseIO.i_SyncUnitWC)
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[(* The meters are fed from the gas panel; while that panel's EtherCAT sync
   unit is down neither its valves nor its flow readbacks can be trusted, so a
   flow setpoint must not be issued. *)
F_BronkhorstMFM_ILK := i_xPanelFieldbusOK;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>
